1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,586
Most of the day, this screen is off.

2
00:00:03,636 --> 00:00:07,200
Turn it on, and it sells you something.

3
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:11,381
Today turns the Fire TV into something else.

4
00:00:11,431 --> 00:00:20,610
A window that follows the light and the weather — it's raining in Brooklyn, so the tiger has its umbrella.

5
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:22,438
One step that's hers.

6
00:00:22,488 --> 00:00:25,050
The whole family, at a glance.

7
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:35,600
It opens already knowing what she's been letting slide.

8
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:43,900
She talks to her phone, however it comes out.

9
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:47,828
She never touches the television.

10
00:00:47,878 --> 00:00:51,700
A few seconds later, it catches up on its own.

11
00:00:53,929 --> 00:00:56,684
Something she keeps putting off.

12
00:00:56,734 --> 00:00:58,524
It asks one question.

13
00:00:58,574 --> 00:01:00,979
One — because two is a form.

14
00:01:05,143 --> 00:01:12,093
Ask it something it doesn't know, and it looks it up, then reads what it found against this family.

15
00:01:18,143 --> 00:01:20,592
Somewhere warm for an eight-month-old.

16
00:01:20,642 --> 00:01:25,393
It skips the place that's closed on Saturdays, and hands the choice back.

17
00:01:32,457 --> 00:01:38,631
Underneath, it's broken down, each step with the moment it fits into.

18
00:01:38,681 --> 00:01:41,607
But she only ever gets one a day.

19
00:01:48,329 --> 00:01:54,518
Press right on the remote, and the same thing opens on the big screen.

20
00:01:54,568 --> 00:01:58,529
When, what it costs, whether it suits a baby.

21
00:02:02,829 --> 00:02:06,324
It follows the day, morning to night.

22
00:02:06,374 --> 00:02:08,529
At night, it rests too.

23
00:02:09,129 --> 00:02:10,408
No shopping.

24
00:02:10,458 --> 00:02:11,295
No feed.

25
00:02:11,345 --> 00:02:13,179
No keeping score.

26
00:02:15,129 --> 00:02:15,883
Today.

27
00:02:15,933 --> 00:02:20,979
A small tiger who keeps today for you.
